# Keep the build context small and keep secrets out of image layers.
#
# A .env file copied into a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# `docker history` survives deletion of the running container. Nothing below belongs in
# an image.

.git
.gitignore
.idea
*.iml
.vscode

# Secrets and local overrides. Never in a layer.
docker/env/*.env
!docker/env/*.env.example
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/application-local.properties

# Build output of OTHER modules. The Dockerfile copies exactly one jar, named by the
# SERVICE build argument, so everything else is noise that invalidates the cache.
**/target/classes
**/target/test-classes
**/target/generated-sources
**/target/maven-status
**/target/surefire-reports
**/target/*.jar.original

# Documentation and diagrams
*.md
architecture/
docs/
